moira (0.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Package 1: local History foundation and privacy-safe persistence — an
    on-device, race-free SQLite store under the user state directory with
    integrity checks; history never leaves the machine.
  * Package 2: History interface with selectable 24h/7d/30d/90d ranges and
    per-service filters, quota series with reset transitions, and
    local-time rendering.
  * Package 3: exact daily token totals and summaries from official Codex
    account usage, typed availability semantics and semantic schema v4
    invariants — Claude remains percentage-only with no estimates.
  * Package 4: exact statistics and activity indicators with
    capability-aware rendering — exact values are shown only where the
    provider contract supports them, never generic balances.
  * Package 5: complementary UX — per-provider collection toggles and
    typed alert rules, native desktop and NTFY notification channels with
    deduplicated exhaustion, recovery, reset and error events, sanitized
    diagnostics with copy actions, deterministic CSV/JSON export, history
    deletion, manual update checks with strict SemVer parsing, compact
    mode, and persisted settings (configuration schema v3).
  * Package 6: 0.3.0 release integration and artifact hygiene,
    privacy-minimal agent activity visibility through owned Claude Code
    and Hermes hooks and the documented Codex app-server protocol with
    hashed identities, multi-turn correction, and Debian policy compliance
    with reproducible packaging; publication remains deferred.

